/// The contracts component `audit-log` (Audit log) implements.
pub trait AuditLog {
    /// Verify the audit chain
    ///
    /// The route GET /api/audit/verify takes an optional tenant, which must be the tenant resolved from the host and session: any other is refused as tenant-mismatch and recorded as an audit entry (TEN-1140). It answers intact, and when the chain is broken first-break, the sequence number of the first line that no longer chains, and reason. The caller needs the capability audit-read, which the owner holds.
    ///
    /// Postconditions:
    ///
    /// - A log from which an entry was removed, or in which an entry was altered, is reported as broken, with the sequence number of the first line that no longer chains (OBS-007).
    /// - The route answers a principal that holds the capability audit-read and no other; it checks the chain from the first line of the tenant's audit trail and reports how many lines it read, how many chained and how many were written before the chain existed.
    /// - The head of the chain is not yet anchored in the platform audit store and expiry keeps no checkpoint, so a chain shortened at its newest end is not reported as broken (OBS-1216, D-6208, WG-5247).
    ///
    /// Authorisation: public, scheme session, the tenant's policies decide. A principal whose policies permit the operation
    ///
    /// Idempotent: repeating a call has the effect of making it once.
    ///
    /// Contract `verify-audit-chain`, reference CT-128.
    fn verify_audit_chain(
        &self,
        request: VerifyAuditChainRequest,
    ) -> impl std::future::Future<Output = Result<VerifyAuditChainResponse, VerifyAuditChainError>> + Send;
}

